Q: Idiomatic way to implement capability discovery on include in C++ A: <p>For self-registration, take a look at what Google Test does: from</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>TEST(Fix, Tst)
{ my code }
</code></pre>
<p>it generates code like</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>class Fix_Tst_Test{
    void TestBody() override;
    static ::testing::TestInfo *const test_info_ __attribute__((unused));
};
::testing::TestInfo *const Fix_Tst_Test::test_info_
    = ::testing::internal::MakeAndRegisterTestInfo(
        &quot;Fix&quot;,
        &quot;Tst&quot;,
        // other parameters
    );
void Fix_Tst_Test::TestBody()
{ my code }
</code></pre>
<p>The registration is done by the function called to initialize the static member, which happens before <code>main()</code> is called.</p>

Q: Linking php into html (beginner) A: <p>Not sure exactly what you did? It should work with the form action.</p>
<p>In fact the php code you've got won't do much in response to clicking on an &quot;a href&quot; hyperlink, because that only generates a HTTP GET request, and your php code is programmed to output something when it receives a POST request instead. Your form will send a POST, when submitted.</p>
<p>Can you edit the question to show what you tried, I suspect it would be a an easy fix if we could see it.</p>
<p>But basically you should just have ended up with</p>
<pre><code>&lt;form action=&quot;http://localhost/playlisty.php&quot; method=&quot;post&quot;&gt;
  &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;buttonm&quot; value=&quot;Show&quot;&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: npm run test task in VSCode suddenly injecting with yarn A: <p>My <code>.vscode/settings.json</code> that worked was:</p>
<pre><code>{
  &quot;npm.autoDetect&quot;: &quot;on&quot;,
  &quot;npm.scriptRunner&quot;: &quot;bun&quot;
}
</code></pre>

Q: NavHostFragment not resolved (AndroidX) A: <p>For Java:</p>
<pre><code>dependencies {
def nav_version = &quot;2.3+&quot;

implementation &quot;androidx.navigation:navigation-fragment:$nav_version&quot;
implementation &quot;androidx.navigation:navigation-ui:$nav_version&quot;

}
</code></pre>
<p>For Kotlin:</p>
<pre><code>dependencies {
def nav_version = &quot;2.3+&quot;

implementation &quot;androidx.navigation:navigation-fragment-ktx:$nav_version&quot;
implementation &quot;androidx.navigation:navigation-ui-ktx:$nav_version&quot;

}
</code></pre>
